			"widgets_values":[
				"integrated_multimodal_description: A poetic Chinese ink-wash aesthetic cinematic piece, featuring a young woman in traditional Hanfu within a classical Jiangnan garden during a gentle rain, with soft diffused lighting, muted celadon and ink-gray color palette, shallow depth of field, and subtle anamorphic lens flare from paper lanterns. The video opens on a medium shot of the woman standing under a curved wooden eaves, raindrops falling in steady threads beyond the shelter.\n\n[Shot 1] The camera holds in a static medium shot as the woman, wearing a layered pale celadon-green Hanfu with flowing wide sleeves and delicate silver embroidery along the collar, lifts her right hand and extends it palm-up beyond the eaves, allowing raindrops to fall onto her palm, her eyes gently lowered, a faint peaceful smile on her lips, her long black hair tied with a simple jade hairpin, a few loose strands dampened by mist.\n\n[Shot 2] At 00:03.500, the camera cuts to a close-up tracking shot slowly panning right with small amplitude at slow speed, following a single raindrop as it slides down a carved wooden pillar and falls into a stone basin filled with lotus leaves, creating a tiny ripple, the woman's blurred Hanfu sleeve visible in the foreground, soft rain sounds filling the space.\n\n[Shot 3] At 00:07.000, the camera cuts to a wide shot from behind as the woman walks slowly along a stone path through the garden, her wide sleeves swaying gently with each step, holding a pale paper umbrella that is now open above her, rain pattering on the paper surface, mist rising from the wet stone and moss, a distant pavilion half-hidden in fog, the scene fading into soft ink-wash atmosphere.\n\noverall_soundscape: The soft, steady patter of rain on wooden eaves and stone, the gentle plink of droplets falling into a water basin, the faint rustle of silk Hanfu sleeves, distant birdsong muted by rain, and a subtle ambient hum of wind through garden trees.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: A solo guqin (Chinese seven-string zither) piece with slow, resonant plucked notes and generous sustain, accompanied by a faint bamboo flute that enters in the final shot, conveying quiet contemplation and harmony with nature.\n",
				1344,
				768,
				73
			],
